    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups against struggling arms. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (66.67) lead our offensive charge, benefiting significantly from a high-upside matchup against Ethan Pecko and his 5.95 xERA. Their high scores are buoyed by strong park factors and the luxury of hitting in the top three of the order, where their efficiency is maximized. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (71.28) remains a foundational anchor; despite a standard matchup against Bryce Elder, his refined consistency keeps his floor high, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.57) continues to be a mandatory start as he capitalizes on a favorable xERA environment against Seth Lugo.\n\nOur strategy for stolen bases remains aggressive, though we face notable headwinds with elite arms on the mound. **Sam Antonacci** (46.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (49.47) are facing Jacob deGrom and Paul Skenes, respectively\u2014two pitchers whose elite skill sets suppress base-stealing opportunities and overall efficiency. The optimizer kept **Miguel Vargas** (39.60) on the bench, as his proximity to the sub-40 danger zone made him the odd man out; he trailed **Jackson Merrill** due to the latter\u2019s superior dynamic platoon advantage, though **Miguel Vargas** remains a top-tier depth option if any last-minute lineup changes arise. \n\nRisk management is paramount today given the number of \"Lineup Pending\" designations across our roster. While **Liam Hicks** (55.40) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.66) offer solid output, their projections are sensitive to final batting order placements. We are monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** (61.72) closely, as he remains our most reliable anchor despite park-factor volatility. With **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages** sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** to provide the necessary secondary production to support our high-end talent. Investors should note that **Drake Baldwin** faces a steep challenge against Tyler Glasnow; while he remains in the lineup, his utility is strictly capped by the quality of the opposing starter.",
